    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d376-a4">

                <pb facs="0495" n="415" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg415"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure 3.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The colonial secretary to Captain
                    Gallagher</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Government Office</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Vincent</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-05-26"><hi rendition="#italic">May 26,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am directed by his excellency the
                    governor to convey to you his cordial thanks and acceptance of the kind offer
                    made by you this morning in person on behalf of the United States Government to
                    defray the expense of the employment of some 100 to 200 of the eruption
                    refugees, with a view to affording them employment and expediting the landing of
                    the cargo now being put on shore from the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dixie.</hi></p>
                <p>I have, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward J. Cameron</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Colonial Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
